  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the goal is to establish a strong baseline while gaining information about multiple key design dimensions simultaneously. config_048 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) combines the strongest available components: a purpose-built single-cell foundation model (scgpt) for RNA, a large pretrained ViT-L for images, transformer-based aggregation for expressive multi-profile integration, and weighted fusion to let the model learn modality importance. If this performs well, it confirms the multimodal + strong-encoder direction and I can ablate individual components in later experiments. If it underperforms, it signals that complexity (transformer aggregation, ViT-L, or weighted fusion) may be harmful, directing exploration toward simpler alternatives. This single experiment reduces uncertainty across four major design axes (model type, encoder quality, aggregation, fusion) and sets a high bar for the remaining 9 experiments."
}

